{"absent":["Per-CPU protection wrapper internals and ordering guarantees beyond wide-operation preemption handling.","Page-table allocation, locking, TLB maintenance and fault handling outside install and free helpers.","Perf event subsystem behavior beyond register capture and user-register accessor.","Translation register programming sequence and runtime enablement of fourth and fifth levels.","Stage-two mapping lifecycle and realm shared-protection value selection.","Guarded-stack and permission-indirection runtime use beyond template and table definitions.","Swapper directory layout and dedicated swapper installer behavior."],"dossier":"D11","findings":[{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/percpu.h::_pcp_protect"],"text":"Offers per-CPU atomic exchange and compare-and-exchange across one, two, four and eight byte widths behind a common protection wrapper, with a dedicated 64-bit compare-and-exchange name mapped to the eight byte form."},{"kind":"lock","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/percpu.h::_pcp_protect"],"text":"The 128-bit per-CPU compare-and-exchange runs with preemption disabled without tracing, operates on the calling CPU copy obtained as a raw pointer, invokes a CPU-local wide compare primitive, restores preemption, and yields the previously stored wide value."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/percpu.h::__per_cpu_offset","arch/arm64/include/asm/percpu.h::per_cpu_offset","arch/arm64/include/asm/percpu.h::this_cpu_ptr","arch/arm64/include/asm/percpu.h::__this_cpu_read","arch/arm64/include/asm/percpu.h::__this_cpu_write"],"text":"CPU offset lookup forwards to the hypervisor per-CPU offset helper, while current-CPU pointer access and current-CPU read and write access are direct aliases of their raw counterparts, adding no extra checks in these fragments."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/perf_event.h::perf_arch_bpf_user_pt_regs","arch/arm64/include/asm/perf_event.h::perf_arch_fetch_caller_regs"],"text":"Perf helpers expose the user register area from a full register snapshot and synthesize caller state by storing the supplied return address as program counter, the current frame address in the frame register, the current stack pointer, and a privileged handler processor state."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/pgalloc.h::pud_populate","arch/arm64/include/asm/pgalloc.h::p4d_populate","arch/arm64/include/asm/pgalloc.h::pgd_populate"],"text":"Upper-level table installers create table descriptors with accessed tracking enabled and choose unprivileged execute-never for the initial address space and privileged execute-never otherwise, translating the child table address from kernel virtual to physical during installation."},{"kind":"state_machine","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/pgalloc.h::__p4d_populate.alt_1","arch/arm64/include/asm/pgalloc.h::__p4d_populate.alt_2","arch/arm64/include/asm/pgalloc.h::__pgd_populate.alt_1","arch/arm64/include/asm/pgalloc.h::__pgd_populate.alt_2","arch/arm64/include/asm/pgalloc.h::pud_free"],"text":"Fourth-level install and free plus top-level install depend on whether the corresponding table level is enabled; one build silently skips disabled installs and frees, the alternate build reports a compile-time fault for disabled installs, and upper-directory free is defined as doing nothing when the fourth level is off."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/pgalloc.h::pmd_populate_kernel","arch/arm64/include/asm/pgalloc.h::pmd_populate"],"text":"Middle-level installers enforce address-space separation by debug-checking that the kernel variant is used only for the initial address space and the generic variant never for it, both installing table descriptors with accessed tracking while selecting unprivileged execute-never for kernel tables and privileged execute-never for generic tables."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/pgtable.h::set_p4d","arch/arm64/include/asm/pgtable.h::set_pgd"],"text":"Fourth and